    <string name="background">Stay connected in the background</string>
    <string name="background_off">Off: messages arrive while the app is open or briefly in the background.</string>
    <string name="background_on">On: messages and calls arrive even when the app is closed. Uses some battery.</string>
    <string name="background_q">Receive in the background?</string>
    <string name="background_text1">Conversa then stays connected to the relays. Messages and calls arrive immediately – even when the app is closed or the phone is in standby. No Google service is used.</string>
    <string name="background_text2" formatted="false">🔋 Battery: this uses extra power, roughly an estimated 1–5 % per day. The exact amount depends on the phone, the network (Wi-Fi uses less than mobile data) and the number of messages. Reason: the phone briefly checks every few minutes whether the connection is still up.</string>
    <string name="background_text3">Android shows a permanent notice in the notification bar for this. You can hide it in the system settings. With Tor, Orbot must also run in the background.</string>
